From: mothershipOS
Subject: [PATCH] hexagonrpcd: a writable sensors registry, fremove, unsupported calls are not fatal

The SLPI's sensor process (Qualcomm SEE, nio/SM8250) maintains its registry over FastRPC like on Android:
- it writes persist/sensors/registry/sns_reg_version and registry groups, and removes files it rewrites. The served
  tree is read-only, so -w DIR adds a writable copy of the persist registry: fopen for writing, fwrite and fremove,
  confined to persist/sensors/registry/{registry/<file>,sns_reg_version} (".." resolved) and mapped into DIR.
  Removing anything else is ignored (reported as done); sns_reg_version is also served for reading.
- an unsupported call ended the listener loop, so the daemon exited at the first one and the sensor process
  crashed on its next registry access. It now gets its error result and the listener carries on.
- the "invalid number of input numbers" message names the method.

diff --git a/hexagonrpcd/apps_std.c b/hexagonrpcd/apps_std.c
